  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A radar detector is used to measure the speed of a car. The car is moving with a speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> towards the detector.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The detector emits microwaves of frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f\"></span> and speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c\"></span>. Which of the following is the change in frequency of the microwaves measured at the detector after reflection by the car?<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{-2vf}{c}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{-vf}{c}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{vf}{c}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2vf}{c}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
